id: pm-rust-context-intents
title: Native core context intents and explicit section selection
description: "Implement orient and handoff intent defaults, section selection, activity limits and budget receipts; certify deeper context and relationship packets against pm 2026.11.5."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: native,oracle,orientation
created_at: "2026-11-06T09:15:56.754Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T11:29:42.862Z"
assignee: codex-astra
claim_principal: codex-astra
author: codex-astra
acceptance_criteria: "JSON and TOON bytes, status and stderr match the oracle on generated non-git trackers and public tracker copies; retain typed calendar and memory refusals; focused tests fail on behavioral revert; record latency and differential counts."
parent: pm-rust-s6j4
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T09:28:14.771Z",codex-astra,"Implemented core intent preparation, section selection, activity bounds and intent receipts. Current-oracle exploration identified three inherited context drifts: bounded activity excludes timestamps at or after the read clock; test health covers all matching active items and declares its scope; TOON auto-tables choose compact list/null columns only when shorter. Bringing these paths to the requested November contract before running the public-copy corpus."
  "2026-11-06T09:44:02.034Z",codex-astra,"Public-copy packet differential exposed the newer required-root-evidence-first-v1 ordering, reserved root-edge budget, root-edge priority and bounded-relationship omission receipt. Porting those native packet semantics as part of this slice, including updated producer fingerprints. No legacy packet result is being counted as current-oracle evidence."
  "2026-11-06T10:08:53.263Z",codex-astra,"Generated intent comparisons passed before the final expanded matrix. Public-copy exploration exposed the distinction between compact intent estimates and complete JSON wire ceilings, now handled by the shared output-budget path. Current dependency packets also require root-evidence-first ordering and revised refusal text; preserving the existing bounded retry test while eliminating repeated rendering of identical packets."
  "2026-11-06T10:37:55.523Z",codex-astra,"The expanded current-oracle corpus passed 306 intent/section/continuation comparisons. The broader suite passed 32 of 33 tests; the remaining debug retry timeout motivated sharing exact rendered-cost measurements across budget recovery probes. All library tests except the old ordering fingerprint fixture passed; that fixture is updated for the already-differentially-verified ordering. Added equal-sign option and token-budget alias refusal cases, plus lossless compact-table edge coverage. Strict Clippy and all 41 binary unit tests pass."
  "2026-11-06T10:44:49.532Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert proofs passed in a disposable text-source copy: disabling only intent preparation failed core_intent_boundaries_and_budget_receipts and context_intents_and_sections_match_current_oracle; disabling compact columns failed current_context_tables_keep_ambiguous_cells_lossless; restoring the prior packet implementation failed relationship_packets_match_oracle. Every run reached named test failures, with no compilation-only false positive. The package worktree stayed fixed; positive reruns follow."
  "2026-11-06T11:18:17.403Z",codex-astra,"The final expanded run exceeded its 30-minute linked-run timeout under shared-host oracle startup cost; it is not counted as a pass. Split the identical rich, empty and wide evidence matrices into independent tests, retaining every comparison while keeping the fixed two-worker ceiling. Increased the linked-run timeout to one hour. Each split test is included in the behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-11-06T11:29:42.852Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert validation passed for all five new tests: core intent unit, rich/empty/wide-wire integration fixtures, and lossless compact-table unit. The upgraded relationship packet differential also fails against the previous packet implementation. The scratch runner requires named assertion failures and rejects compilation-only failures. Clippy passed with all targets and features and warnings denied; the final positive differential run is underway."
